    "recommendations": "Ensuring the front driveway and access road remain clear of obstructions could support unimpeded entry and exit for emergency apparatus, particularly given the single point of access serving the property. Maintaining adequate turning and staging space along the driveway would assist larger vehicles in maneuvering during an incident. Clearly marking the address at the street frontage could improve responder navigation during initial approach. The dense vegetation near the access corridor and rear of the property may limit visibility and movement for personnel working around the detached structure, so keeping travel pathways to and around both structures as open as practical could enhance operational effectiveness."
