    "recommendations": "Reducing the density of shrub cover immediately surrounding the structure and creating separation between ground-level brush and any overhanging tree canopy could meaningfully reduce fuel continuity and ladder fuel pathways near the building. Thinning vegetation within the immediate structure perimeter and clearing brush directly adjacent to exterior walls and under eaves would support defensible space and may reduce structure exposure. Where tree clusters exist near the structure, removing low-hanging limbs and reducing understory shrub density beneath the canopy could interrupt vertical fuel continuity. Managing vegetation along the single access route, including trimming encroaching brush and maintaining adequate width and vertical clearance, would support firefighter access and improve evacuation conditions. Given that a single access route serves the property, keeping that corridor clear of vegetation encroachment should be considered a priority. Continuing long-term vegetation management across the property perimeter could improve overall wildfire resilience and suppression support opportunities."
